# .cursorrules — Nexus RPG Engine

## Project Identity
Local-first, CPU-only AI RPG Engine. Two modes: Architect (knowledge graph builder)
and Actor (interactive narrative). Runs on homelab hardware via docker-compose.

## Hard Constraints — NEVER violate these
- NO cloud services, hosted APIs, or managed databases of any kind
- NO GPU/CUDA code. All inference runs on CPU via Ollama GGUF models
- NO OpenAI, Pinecone, AWS, Azure, Chroma, Weaviate, or any SaaS alternative
- Models in use: mistral:7b or llama3.1:8b (Q4_K_M), llava:7b, nomic-embed-text
- Target CPU: Intel Xeon E3 class. Always minimize blocking operations

## Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 14 (App Router), React, React Flow, Tailwind CSS, TypeScript
- Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.11+), async throughout, Pydantic v2
- LLM Calls: httpx → Ollama REST API. Use instructor library for structured JSON output
- Vector DB: LanceDB embedded (no server process). Always filter by location_key metadata
- State: world_state.json is the single source of graph truth (nodes + edges)
- Branching: Chronos engine — ZSTD-compressed RFC 6902 JSON Patch delta commits
- Deployment: docker-compose with named volumes, bridge network

## Directory Layout
nexus-engine/
├── backend/
│   ├── main.py               # FastAPI app, lifespan, CORS
│   ├── config.py             # Pydantic Settings (reads .env)
│   ├── llm_client.py         # Ollama HTTP wrapper (generate, embed, vision)
│   ├── world_state.py        # Async read/write helpers for world_state.json
│   ├── rag.py                # LanceDB wrapper with metadata-filtered search
│   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── architect_router.py
│   │   ├── actor_router.py
│   │   ├── chronos_router.py
│   │   └── import_router.py
│   ├── chronos/
│   │   └── commit_engine.py  # ChronosEngine, ChronosCommit dataclass
│   ├── pipeline/
│   │   └── import_pipeline.py  # Vision + text import, async with Semaphore
│   ├── axiom/
│   │   └── engine.py         # Deterministic constraint validator (NO LLM calls)
│   └── prompts/
│       ├── architect_mode.py
│       ├── actor_mode.py     # FreytagStage, injectors, temperatures
│       └── vision_mode.py
├── frontend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── map/page.tsx      # React Flow mind map
│   │   ├── play/page.tsx     # Actor mode chat + Freytag UI
│   │   └── timeline/page.tsx # Chronos DAG branch viewer
│   └── components/
├── data/                     # gitignored — Docker volume mount target
│   ├── world_state.json
│   ├── lancedb/
│   └── chronos/
└── docker-compose.yml

## Code Rules
- Every Python function that touches I/O must be async
- Never block the asyncio event loop. Use asyncio.to_thread() for sync libs (LanceDB, PIL)
- Return 202 + job_id immediately for any operation >1 second. Use BackgroundTasks + SSE
- All Ollama calls go through llm_client.py, never raw httpx in route handlers
- LanceDB queries MUST include a WHERE location_key filter. Never do unfiltered vector scans
- Pydantic v2 models for all request/response bodies. Use Field(pattern=...) for IDs
- Node IDs: snake_case with type prefix: char_ | loc_ | item_ | org_ | event_ | concept_

## When generating code
- Write complete, runnable files — no placeholder TODOs or stub functions
- Include all imports at the top of each file
- Use Python logging, never print()
- Add a brief docstring to every class and public function